1
00:00:00,170 --> 00:00:02,353
The agent says the job is finished.

2
00:00:02,353 --> 00:00:05,212
But the spreadsheet is still shared outside the team.

3
00:00:05,212 --> 00:00:07,712
And a customer email is waiting to send.

4
00:00:07,712 --> 00:00:10,328
Counterstep picks up after the overstep.

5
00:00:10,738 --> 00:00:12,881
Run logs can show the overstep.

6
00:00:12,881 --> 00:00:15,971
They do not restore the state the operator intended.

7
00:00:15,971 --> 00:00:20,605
Counterstep is for the moment after a completed agent run exceeded its authority.

8
00:00:20,605 --> 00:00:25,699
It inspects current state, applies only reversible repairs, then checks again.

9
00:00:26,149 --> 00:00:28,268
The incident trace is synthetic.

10
00:00:28,268 --> 00:00:30,615
The recovery execution is real.

11
00:00:30,615 --> 00:00:32,667
Missing fields remain unknown.

12
00:00:32,667 --> 00:00:37,808
Gemini receives minimized facts and current findings, then proposes a cited plan.

13
00:00:37,808 --> 00:00:40,981
Deterministic code decides whether that plan may run.

14
00:00:41,411 --> 00:00:44,578
The Recovery Test Rack makes that contract visible.

15
00:00:44,578 --> 00:00:49,983
E1 is the canonical repair: revoke one external share and cancel one queued email.

16
00:00:49,983 --> 00:00:51,696
E2 proves restraint.

17
00:00:51,696 --> 00:00:55,238
E3 refuses to describe a delivered email as recalled.

18
00:00:55,238 --> 00:00:57,437
E4 re-inspects stale state.

19
00:00:57,927 --> 00:01:01,245
Now watch E1 run on the public Cloud Run deployment.

20
00:01:01,245 --> 00:01:03,652
This is one continuous execution.

21
00:01:03,652 --> 00:01:06,395
There are no cuts between the click and the receipt.

22
00:01:06,395 --> 00:01:09,045
Two current-state inspections come first.

23
00:01:09,045 --> 00:01:12,958
Gemini, through Google ADK, proposes the bounded plan.

24
00:01:12,958 --> 00:01:15,539
Code admits it before either write can happen.

25
00:01:15,539 --> 00:01:20,978
Then Counterstep revokes the share, cancels the delivery, and reads both resources again.

26
00:01:20,978 --> 00:01:24,925
Every accepted event and state transition is retained in Firestore.

27
00:01:25,455 --> 00:01:26,979
The contract matched.

28
00:01:26,979 --> 00:01:28,854
Both closure goals passed.

29
00:01:28,854 --> 00:01:34,988
The ledger shows two writes, six tool calls, one admitted plan, and all twelve source events accounted for.

30
00:01:34,988 --> 00:01:40,740
The closure digest binds this result to its trace, authority, tool results, and final state.

31
00:01:41,210 --> 00:01:43,907
Recovery also means knowing when to stop.

32
00:01:43,907 --> 00:01:47,079
With E3, the message has already been delivered.

33
00:01:47,079 --> 00:01:51,737
It may revoke the spreadsheet share, but reports the delivery as not reversible.

34
00:01:51,737 --> 00:01:54,910
With E4, the first write meets a stale version.

35
00:01:54,910 --> 00:02:00,051
The agent re-inspects both resources and uses its one allowed replacement plan.

36
00:02:00,051 --> 00:02:01,985
No stale write is retried.

37
00:02:02,495 --> 00:02:04,838
Next.js runs on Cloud Run.

38
00:02:04,838 --> 00:02:10,334
Google ADK connects Gemini 3.5 Flash Lite to five bounded server-side tools.

39
00:02:10,334 --> 00:02:12,822
Firestore stores state and receipts.

40
00:02:12,822 --> 00:02:14,626
Gemini chooses a plan.

41
00:02:14,626 --> 00:02:17,845
Code owns authority, transitions, and closure.

42
00:02:17,845 --> 00:02:22,916
Without a valid Gemini execution, Counterstep fails closed and writes nothing.

43
00:02:23,386 --> 00:02:25,940
Here is the same deployment in Google Cloud.

44
00:02:25,940 --> 00:02:33,162
The health response reports Cloud Run, Firestore, Vertex AI, Google ADK TypeScript, and the exact Gemini model.

45
00:02:33,162 --> 00:02:38,417
The public .run.app address and Cloud Run revision tie this demo to the hosted service.

46
00:02:38,907 --> 00:02:45,048
Counterstep's new recovery system is documented separately from the Agent Receipt foundation it reuses.

47
00:02:45,558 --> 00:02:49,678
When another agent says it is done, Counterstep checks what is true now.

48
00:02:49,678 --> 00:02:53,662
It repairs what is still reversible and leaves a receipt for the fix.

49
00:02:54,252 --> 00:02:56,642
Every overstep gets a counterstep.
